# Local development: leave DATABASE_URL unset (the app uses PGlite in ./data/pglite) and sign in as the
# development user: `npm run dev` sets KASBOEK_DEV_AUTH=1 for you. Nothing else is needed.

# Real sign-in (Supabase Auth). Both values are public by design (Project settings > API).
# SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# Hosted database: the app's role through the pooler (port 6543), TLS on. The password is set by hand,
# see docs/auth-setup.md. Never commit it.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://kasboek_app.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
